  "tour": {
    "title": "What happened",
    "steps": [
      {
        "title": "The path of a login",
        "body_html": "<p>The web and the app call the gateway, which sends each <code>POST /login</code> to the identity service. It checks the session in Redis and the credentials in the user database.</p>",
        "focus": {
          "nodes": [
            "web",
            "app",
            "gateway",
            "auth"
          ],
          "edges": [
            "e-web-gw",
            "e-app-gw",
            "e-gw-auth"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "10:42 · the pool runs dry",
        "body_html": "<p>Version 5.4 stopped using the cache: every login goes to the database and the 400-connection pool fills up in two minutes.</p>",
        "focus": {
          "nodes": [
            "auth",
            "users-db"
          ],
          "edges": [
            "e-auth-db"
          ]
        },
        "select": "users-db"
      },
      {
        "title": "How far it reaches",
        "body_html": "<p>Press <b>✺ Impact</b> on the identity service: everything that needs to log in goes down with it.</p>",
        "focus": {
          "nodes": [
            "auth"
          ]
        },
        "select": "auth"
      },
      {
        "title": "11:02 · the storm",
        "body_html": "<p>After the rollback, clients retry without waiting and saturate Redis. The failover to the replica resolves it at 11:08.</p>",
        "focus": {
          "nodes": [
            "auth",
            "redis"
          ],
          "edges": [
            "e-auth-redis"
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "title": "What changes",
        "body_html": "<p>Load testing in CI, retries with exponential backoff, a pool alert and an automatic canary.</p>",
        "focus": {
          "nodes": [
            "acciones"
          ]
        },
        "select": "acciones"
      }
    ]
  }
